  "sections": {
    "review": {
      "summary": "OWN-071: capture weeks 1-7 with the worker. Read-only check 2026-11-22: weeks 1-7 (107 scheduled games) have no nfl_game rows; week 8 has ESPN records only; NFL records from week 9. catchup.recover_week reads NFL records only from first_nfl_period (9), a rule meant to protect week 8's reviewed ESPN record; weeks 1-7 have no record to protect, and OWN-041 makes the NFL API primary. data/live-captures is 431 MB of its 5 GiB limit.",
      "files": [
        "services/worker/src/arbit_worker/catchup.py",
        "tests/integration/test_catchup.py",
        "docs/engineering/catch-up.md"
      ]
    },
    "plan": {
      "summary": "Add stored_games(uow, season, period); run() passes never_captured when a week has no stored game; recover_week reads NFL records when never_captured or period >= nfl_from. Split the week-8 test into a stored-week case (no NFL) and a never-captured case (NFL owns plays). Verify with a recorded mutation check, full live-class checks, a restored copy, then arbit-worker catchup --from-period 1 on arbit_local (worker may keep running; it already has the scope fix).",
      "files": [
        "services/worker/src/arbit_worker/catchup.py",
        "tests/integration/test_catchup.py",
        "docs/engineering/catch-up.md"
      ]
    },
    "implementation": {
      "summary": "catchup.stored_games; recover_week never_captured parameter; run passes it per week. Tests: test_a_stored_week_before_the_nfl_lane_began_keeps_its_espn_record and test_a_week_never_captured_gets_the_nfl_record_before_the_nfl_lane_began (13 catch-up tests). Guide NFL-records line, status line, changelog entry.",
      "files": [
        "services/worker/src/arbit_worker/catchup.py",
        "tests/integration/test_catchup.py",
        "docs/engineering/catch-up.md"
      ]
    },
    "validation": {
      "summary": "Observed exit 0: mutation-never-captured (with the never_captured clause removed, the never-captured test fails; restored), foundation, live-replay, runtime-check (1343 backend tests with PostgreSQL), web-check; re-run after the status result line. Real data: dry run on a restored copy planned exactly 107 unstored games in weeks 1-7; the copy run recovered 107, 0 failed, 19,780 play revisions, all 107 NFL finals, week 8 untouched; the same run on arbit_local recovered 107, 0 failed, nothing remaining. Database now: weeks 1-10 complete (week 8 ESPN-only by design), week 11 live, schedule scope (2, 11); worker logged no error codes in the following 20 minutes. Copy dropped.",
      "files": []
